TITLE:: CompressorHistoryView
summary:: the last eight seconds of level and gain change
categories:: Libraries>Compressor
related:: Classes/Compressor, Classes/CompressorPanel, Classes/CompressorCurveView

DESCRIPTION::
One frame per meter reply, newest at the right, on FxMeter's dB ruler: the
input filled, the output as a blue line, the gain change in orchid hanging from
0 dB (in up mode, rising from the floor), and the threshold as an orchid line
across it. Where the detector is over the line (under it, in up mode) the gap is
tinted orchid, right above the cut it causes. The detector gets a line of its
own when it is not simply the input: an external sidechain, the eq in, or the
rms detector. Under 48 dB the range is a dashed floor.

Before any reply has come it plays a test kick - every half second, -3 dBFS
falling 30 dB in 120 ms onto -36 dBFS - through the current settings, worked
out in numbers with the same gain computer and the same attack and release as
link::Classes/Compressor#*ar:: (link::#*ghostFor::), faint and labelled. When
replies stop it keeps what it had and says strong::no signal::; off, it says
the gain is what it would do.

table::
## drag the line || the threshold (shift: fine)
## double click it || -20 dB
## the wheel on it || 0.5 dB a step
## double click elsewhere || clear it - the test kick comes back
## listens to ... in the caption || the source menu
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: comp
ARGUMENT:: parent

METHOD:: seconds
How much it shows, 8.

METHOD:: floorDb

METHOD:: ghostStep
The test kick's drawing step, in seconds.

METHOD:: ghostFor
One second of the test kick through a compressor's settings.
ARGUMENT:: comp
RETURNS:: [detector, input, output, gain], each an Array of dB, one every code::ghostStep::.

code::
c = Compressor.new; c.preset = \pump;
g = CompressorHistoryView.ghostFor(c);
g[3].minItem;     // the most it cuts the kick, in dB
::

